Carlos Casas, filmmaker and visual artist working across experimental cinema, sound, and installation, made a film and sound piece tracing Lorca's footsteps and memory in Catalonia. Rather than biography, it proposes a sensorial experience connecting the landscapes Lorca visited with his artistic sensibility, exploring memory, time, and the poet's presence in those places.

I provided on-site technical support for the installation which included everything from getting the film to making it work with Bright Sign Player to clean-up wiring.

Shown as part of "Lorca en Cataluña: Yo no he nacido todavía," curated by Francisco Ortuño Millán for Art Hub Collective, Venice 2026.

[Art Hub Collective](https://www.arthubcollective.art/lorca)
